==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term/t|non|steinn||stone}}, from {{etyl|gmq-pro|is}} {{term|lang=gmq-pro|ᛊᛏᚨᛁᚾᚨᛉ|tr=stainaz}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*stainaz||stone}}. Cognate with {{etyl|en|-}} {{term/t|en|stone}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term/t|en|Stein}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term/t|nl|steen}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term/t|da|sten}}, {{etyl|nb|-}} {{term/t|nb|sten}}, {{etyl|nn|-}} {{term/t|nn|stein}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term/t|sv|sten}}, {{etyl|fo|-}} {{term/t|da|steinur}}, {{etyl|fy|-}} {{term/t|fy|stien}}, {{etyl|nds|-}} {{term/t|nds|Steen}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*stāi-||something hard}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/steitn/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|eitn|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|steins|steinar}}

# [[stone]], [[rock]]
# [[stone]], [[pit]], [[pip]] (the seed of certain [[fruit]])
# {{context|medicine|lang=is}} a [[calculus]], a [[stone]]

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-m-s1|st|ei|n|n|i=i}}

